[N 24-24 The Cozy Sleeping Bag]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Optional side trip between Darkshore and Ashenvale: the rest of the Cozy Sleeping Bag chain in one go - the burnt tower in the Barrens, the camp above Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon, the Stonewrought Dam and Thoradin's Wall - for the +3% XP bag at level 24.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffThe Cozy Sleeping Bag|r  -  an optional chapter between Darkshore and 24-25 Ashenvale. You need ... and that note you found (79008) from Alexston Farmstead in your log (chapter 05). Six hand-ins, all at objects: about 10,900 quest XP, the Old Toolbox (a 12-slot bag) and the bag itself, which gives +3% XP from kills and quests. Every quest needs level 14 only and the mobs at the stops are 20-26. Hearth = Sentinel Hill, and this chapter USES it, to get off the dam
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r object positions, guards and mob levels are from the Forever DB. The DB has no roads: the ways between the stops are Classic-era landmarks, and the climbing notes come from Forever web guides read on 12 Nov 2026 - all of that is unverified by play. Well over an hour, most of it running
[OC]|cffffcc00Shape of the trip:|r Astranaar > the Talondeep tunnel > south through Stonetalon into the Barrens > the tower south of Camp Taurajo > back into Stonetalon for the camp above Sun Rock Retreat > tunnel, Astranaar, bird and boat to Menethil > Thelsamar and the dam > Hearthstone > bird to Southshore > Thoradin's Wall > boat back to Auberdine
[OC][A Shaman] Ghost Wolf on every outdoor leg

[OC]|cffffffffAshenvale: Astranaar and the tunnel|r  -  you start at Maestra's Post, where Darkshore ended
[OC]Run east along the road to Astranaar
At flightmaster [TAR4267 Daelyshia], get the [P Astranaar] flightpoint [G34.4,48.0 Ashenvale]
Run south from Astranaar to the cave mouth of the Talondeep Path and through it into Stonetalon Mountains [G42.3,71.0 Ashenvale]

[OC]|cffffffffThrough Stonetalon into the Barrens|r  -  the tunnel comes out in Windshear Crag, in the east of Stonetalon. A Horde tauren, Braug Dimspirit (35), stands at that mouth (78.8,45.7): give him room. The DB shows no Horde guards on the road you are about to take
Follow the road west out of Windshear Crag to the junction where the Alliance NPCs Kaela Shadowspear and Gaxim Rustfizzle stand [G59.9,66.8 Stonetalon Mountains]
[OC]Take the road south from the junction, down through the valleys and out of Stonetalon at its south-east corner. The Horde camp Malaka'jin (71-74,95-99; NPCs 20-30, no guards in the DB) lies west of the road at the very bottom of the zone: do not stop there
[OC]|cFFFF0000The Barrens:|r the road you come out on runs east to the Crossroads, a Horde town with guards. Leave it once you are out of the hills and cut south-east across the savanna; cross the main north-south road well north of Camp Taurajo and stay EAST of it. Camp Taurajo (45,59) has eight level-40 Horde Guards in the DB and one stands by the road (46.3,60.1)
Pass Camp Taurajo two map units or more to the east [G49.0,59.0 The Barrens]
At the burnt tower east of the road, click the Burned-Out Remains at its foot, [QT79008] (1,750 XP), then the Nailed Plank beside it, [QA79192 Stepping Stones] [G46.4,73.9 The Barrens]
[OC]Around the tower: Stormhides, Thunderhawks, Hecklefang Stalkers, Bound Elementals and silithid, all 20-24. Brontus (27, rare) spawns a unit north-east of it

[OC]|cffffffffBack into Stonetalon: the camp above Sun Rock Retreat|r
Run back north the way you came, east of Camp Taurajo again [G49.0,59.0 The Barrens]
[OC]Cut north-west across the savanna to the Stonetalon road, staying well west of the Crossroads, and follow it back up into the mountains
Run back up through Stonetalon to Kaela's junction [G59.9,66.8 Stonetalon Mountains]
[OC]|cFFFF0000Sun Rock Retreat|r is the Horde town west of the junction, guarded by level-38 Stonetalon Grunts; the nearest two stand at the foot of its ramp (49.7,61). The road north to Mirkfallon Lake passes that ramp: keep to the far side of the road and do not stop
Follow the road north-west and north from the junction, past the Sun Rock ramp, to the point where a trail leaves it to the west [G50.9,52.3 Stonetalon Mountains]
Follow the trail west across the mountain to the abandoned camp and click the Pocket Litter on the crate, [QT79192] (1,950 XP) [QA79980 Scramble] [G40.8,52.6 Stonetalon Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (79192):|r the Old Toolbox is a 12-slot bag: equip it. Mining Pick or Farmer's Shovel: either one, vendor it. Keep the Simple Wood and the Flint and Tinder for campfires
[OC]Seen from the valley the camp sits on top of a cliff, so come by the trail, not from Sun Rock or the Charred Vale. Around it: Blackened Basilisks, Rogue Flame Spirits and Bloodfury Harpies (23-24)
From the camp go straight north up the hill to its edge. The Mound of Dirt is on a small ledge just below: jump down onto the ledge and click it, [QT79980] (195 XP) [QA79974 Wet Job] [G39.6,49.8 Stonetalon Mountains]
[OC]Aim the jump: a miss drops you into the ravine and you walk up again from the camp. Scramble's rewards are ranged weapons and ammunition: take any, vendor it

[OC]|cffffffffOut: the tunnel, Astranaar, Auberdine, Menethil|r
[OC]Back along the trail to the road, south past the Sun Rock ramp, then east at Kaela's junction into Windshear Crag
Run back through the Talondeep Path into Ashenvale [G42.3,71.0 Ashenvale]
At [TAR4267 Daelyshia] in Astranaar, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Auberdine]|r [G34.4,48.0 Ashenvale]
Cross the Auberdine dock and take the Menethil boat; get off at Menethil Harbor (the boat carries on to Southshore) [G33.5,40 Darkshore]
At [TAR1571 Shellei Brondir], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r (the game may route it through Ironforge) [G9.5,59.7 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffLoch Modan: the Stonewrought Dam|r
[OC]From Thelsamar run up the west road to the north end of the loch (about 4 minutes) and onto the dam at its west end, where Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII stands (46.1,13.6)
Walk east along the top of the dam, past Mountaineer Angst, to the middle [G48.6,14.4 Loch Modan]
[OC]|cFFFF0000The ledge|r is on the NORTH face, the side with the carved stone heads that looks out over the Wetlands, a little east of Angst (49.4,12.9). Web guides: stand on the wall above the second stone head, look down, find the small camp on a ledge just below the walkway and drop onto it. Do NOT jump past it: below the ledge is the bottom of the dam
Drop onto the ledge and click the Carved Figurine, [QT79974] (2,550 XP) [QA79975 Eagle's Fist] [G49.4,12.9 Loch Modan]
[OC]No guide describes a way back up from the ledge: leave by Hearthstone
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r

[OC]|cffffffffHillsbrad: Thoradin's Wall|r
At [TAR523 Thor], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Southshore]|r (the game routes it; you took the flight path in chapter 08) [G56.5,52.6 Westfall]
[OC]From Southshore run east across Hillsbrad to the wall. Gray Bears and Moss Creepers (20-26) on the way and at the wall
Run to the broken cart that leans into a gap in Thoradin's Wall, on the Hillsbrad side [G87.4,49.7 Hillsbrad Foothills]
[OC]|cffffcc00The climb (web guides, unverified):|r at the cart, jump onto the big cylinder, from it onto the board that sticks out on the right, then up the cart and onto the wall. On the wall, hop up the fallen stones: the low one on the far left first, then the big ones in the middle, then the ones above to the right. At the top a doorway leads through a small room inside the wall; come out on the other side and look right
Click the Messenger Bag hanging on the wall, [QT79975] (2,550 XP) [QA79976 This Must Be The Place] [G22.5,24.1 Arathi Highlands]
Click the Hastily Rolled-Up Satchel on the floor below it, [QT79976] (1,950 XP) - it holds the |cff66ff66Cozy Sleeping Bag|r [G22.5,24.1 Arathi Highlands]
[OC]Do not climb down between the two clicks. The ground on the Arathi side of the wall is level 30-33 (Highland Striders, Plains Creepers): leave the way you came, on the Hillsbrad side
[OC]|cffffcc00Using the bag:|r lay it out outdoors (it does not work in inns or capitals) and lie on it: one stack of Well-Rested per minute, three stacks = +3% XP from kills and quests for 2 hours (Wowhead's news post says 1 hour - unverified). The bag has a one-hour cooldown: nap before every dungeon and long chapter, and again a minute before the buff runs out

[OC]|cffffffffBack to Ashenvale|r
[OC]Run back west to Southshore. One boat line serves Auberdine, Menethil and Southshore: read the sign on the pier, and if the boat calls at Menethil first, stay aboard
Take the boat from the Southshore dock to Auberdine [G50.6,61.0 Hillsbrad Foothills]
At flight master [TAR3841 Caylais Moonfeather], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Astranaar]|r [G36.3,45.6 Darkshore]
[OC]From Astranaar run west along the road to Maestra's Post, where 24-25 Ashenvale starts
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r nothing from this chapter stays in the log. Chapter 26's step at the burnt tower (79008 and Stepping Stones) is already done and shows as complete, and the "Stepping Stones still carried" notes in chapters 26 to 35 no longer apply to you
[NX 24-25 Ashenvale]
]], "Forever Shaman 1-30")
